"state":"open","created_at":"2014-05-10T20:43:04Z","updated_at":"2025-12-12T21:14:43Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":7,"created_at":"2017-02-02T09:37:18Z","updated_at":"2019-09-25T04:57:38Z","closed_at":"2019-09-25T04:57:38Z","author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"- `nvim --version`: `NVIM v0.2.0-498-g050819277`\r\n- Vim (version: ) behaves differently? not sure\r\n- Operating system/version: Arch Linux\r\n- Terminal name/version: cygwin + MinTTY + ssh with x11 forwarding (configured so in `~/.ssh/config`) + tmux (works both within x server and outside of it)\r\n- `$TERM`: `screen-256color`\r\n\r\n### Actual behaviour\r\n\r\nIt takes about 8 seconds for `:Explore` to open netrw window.\r\n\r\n### Expected behaviour\r\n\r\nIt should work instantly, the directory contains about 5 files.\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce using `nvim -u NORC`\r\n\r\n```\r\ntime nvim -u NORC -c 'Explore|q'\r\nnvim -u NORC -c 'Explore|q'  0.06s user 0.01s system 0% cpu 9.102 total\r\n```\r\n\r\nRunning it through `strace` reveals that it spends a great deal of time looking for stuff such as `xclip` and whatnot. `:set clipboard` shows `clipboard=`. It works fast only after I removed the `xclip` binary which I've installed mainly for clipboard via X11 forwarding.","closed_by":{"login":"justinmk","id":1359421,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNTk0MjE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1359421?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk","html_url":"https://github.com/justinmk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/starred{/owne